WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.090
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.250
To first!

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.570
Safe! Safe!

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.790
Is the problem Sato's lead?

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.740
It's the pressure of the pros, isn't it?

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.830
Batting seventh: catcher, Sato.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.620
<i>I can't let it end like this!</i>

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.710
<i>I'll help us tie it in some way!</i>

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:30.810
<i>Again!</i>

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.340
Safe!

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.700
He followed that nicely!

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.770
He's doing quite well!

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.990
<i>Playing half-heartedly because you're scared?</i>

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.420
<i>You're not a pro!</i>

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:15.940
Can I really...

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:18.740
survive as a pro?

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:29.730
Yatabe!

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.470
Have you seen Sato?

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:33.370
Sato?

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.440
I've been looking for him for a while.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.710
I haven't seen him, but...

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:41.860
Well, I think I can guess where he is.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.530
I found you!

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.370
I've been looking for you, Sato.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:52.990
Coach Araki!

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:58.030
It's been decided that you'll wear the starter's mask...

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:00.090
for tomorrow's exhibition game.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.520
The starting pitcher will be Iwai.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:04.470
Do your best!

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.670
W-Wait a minute!

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.780
Don't worry about your mistakes the other day.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:11.110
This is your chance to redeem yourself!

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:14.480
Go with the intent of showing off your true skill!

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:16.640
My true... skill?

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:17.650
My true... skill?

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:20.610
Excessive training is the groundwork for injuries.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:24.020
You are the newcomer whom we expect great things from after all.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.140
Toshi-kun, please give me your autograph!

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:32.680
Please shake my hand!

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:35.370
Toshi-kun!

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:37.080
Here.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.950
Thank you very much!

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.340
Can we get your autograph too?

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.470
Sure.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.140
Grandfather!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.270
Grandmother!

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:06.700
Grandfather, where should we put this up?

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:10.270
Maybe in the hallway? Or perhaps in the guest room?

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.420
I know!

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.570
Let's put it up in our bento shop's storefront!

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:17.640
We'll be able to boast about it everyday!

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.690
True, that's a good spot!

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:21.880
And then everyone will be able to see it.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.830
Stop that!

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:25.560
It's embarrassing!

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:27.700
Oh yeah.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.190
Here, this is for you.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:30.760
What is it?

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:39.630
This charm is famous for its effectiveness.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.190
It can't be... that you went through all the trouble of coming here for that?

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:43.280
It can't be... that you went through all the trouble of coming here for that?

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.220
O-Oh no.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:45.310
O-Oh no.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:50.230
It just so happened that we wanted to go to a hot spring that was close to the camp.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:53.520
And while we were at it, we thought we'd drop by.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.900
And so, we thought we'd give you that too.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:02.730
The truth is, grandfather wanted to keep it a secret and try to surprise you!

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:04.700
Don't say that, grandmother!

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.100
Grandfather.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:07.380
Grandmother.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:09.400
I'm really grateful.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.830
What's this? Thanking us so formally?

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:12.960
That's so distant of you.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:14.750
Exactly!

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.690
A lucky love charm? 

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.820
That charm apparently works really well.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:28.590
Do your best, Toshiya!

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:31.030
When you get a girlfriend, introduce her to us!

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:32.680
W-What are you saying...

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:33.990
W-What are you saying...

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:34.870
you two?

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:39.510
By the way,

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:41.730
come to the exhibition game tomorrow.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:44.780
I'm going to be wearing the starting catcher's mask.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:46.120
That's great!

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.500
Congratulations!

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.290
They're expecting great things from you.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:50.520
Do your best!

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.340
Y-Yeah...

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:52.480
Y-Yeah...

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.810
What's the matter? Aren't you happy?

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.560
No, that's not it.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.580
It's a great chance for a rookie like me.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.270
I'll work as hard as I can.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.380
<i>That's right.</i>

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.960
<i>I have to work hard for my grandfather and grandmother's sake too.</i>

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.930
<i>I absolutely can't make any more mistakes!</i>

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:27.170
<i>Pitcher, Iwai.</i>

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:28.760
<i>Last season,</i>

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.160
<i>he was inserted into the pitching rotation as a rookie.</i>

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.000
<i>He won seven games.</i>

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.100
<i>He throws about 140 km/h.</i>

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:40.720
<i>He has a large assortment of pitches,</i>

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:43.350
<i>and, moreover, his control is excellent.</i>

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:51.330
<i>Whether Iwai-san's characteristics succeed or not in the game depends on the catcher.</i>

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.330
<i>In other words, the game depends on my lead.</i>

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:56.870
<i>This time, for sure...!</i>

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:16.230
Isn't that Yakushiji-kun?

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:17.310
Who's that?

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:20.070
He was Toshiya's teammate.

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:23.990
He was good enough to bat third at Kaido.

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:27.050
Well, he's not as good as our Toshiya though.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:28.860
I see.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:31.570
A showdown between former teammates.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.240
This will be good!

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:39.800
Sato.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:43.750
It's been awhile.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.100
It sure has.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.740
I saw your batting just now.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:48.590
You seem to be in good form.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:51.530
No, that was just batting practice after all.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:55.430
In the Red-White game the other day,
I was easily outmaneuvered by Harada-san.

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:58.460
It can't be helped against Harada-san, can it?

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:00.250
He's Japan's ace after all.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.230
Despite that, it shouldn't happen three times!

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:06.710
So, how are things with you?

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:09.940
You seem to be doing well, genius rookie.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.140
Do your best!

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:12.690
No... that's not...

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.540
Toshi-kun!

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:15.110
Do your best.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:16.170
Toshi-kun!

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:18.030
Look here!

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.200
You're incredibly popular as always.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.200
Well then,

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.730
let's both do our best!

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:27.060
Genius rookie, huh?

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:30.210
Thank you very much!

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:35.660
Yakushiji.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:37.430
Oh, Harada-san.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:40.890
The person you were just talking with... That was Sato Toshiya, right?

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:41.620
Yes.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:43.570
Is he as good as the rumors say?

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:44.950
That's right.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.930
During my high school years, I thought I was lucky...

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:49.620
that he wasn't my enemy.

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:53.070
Well, now he's become your enemy though.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.440
Second!

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:04.170
<i>I can't allow myself to repeat the same mistakes today that I made in the Red-White game.</i>

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:06.500
<i>How is Iwai-san looking?</i>

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:08.360
Short!

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.380
Hey, Sato!

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.510
What are you doing?

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:17.250
I-I'm sorry!

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:18.430
I-I'm sorry!

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.010
Toshiya...

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:27.380
Now taking the field first are the Tokyo Warriors!

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:30.670
Batting first: left fielder, Aota.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:33.890
Batting second: second baseman, Tanioka.

00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:37.040
Batting third: shortstop, Ichikawa.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:40.070
Batting fourth: third baseman, Uchimura.

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:43.210
Batting fifth: right fielder, Rodman.

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:46.960
Batting sixth: first baseman, I. Sunnamu.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:50.340
Batting seventh: center fielder, Kurogome.

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:53.080
Batting eighth: catcher, Sato.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.480
Toshi-kun is a starter!

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.050
He's done it!

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:07.230
<i>Pull yourself together!</i>

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:10.810
I'm counting on you, Sato!

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:13.450
Y-Yes sir!

00:11:13.450 --> 00:11:14.690
Y-Yes sir!

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.080
Play ball!

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:22.260
<i>I absolutely won't let the leadoff batter get on base!</i>

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:25.630
<i>Anyway, we'll carefully plan the location of the pitches.</i>

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:28.290
<i>We'll use Iwai-san's specialty, his slider, here!</i>

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:34.080
<i>The opposite way?</i>

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:37.260
Ball!

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:43.140
<i>Iwai is a pitcher with good control, but...</i>

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:45.130
<i>he has problems at the beginning of games.</i>

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:47.720
Well then, how will you handle this, rookie?

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:51.880
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:54.240
<i>The breaking balls aren't working at all.</i>

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:56.690
<i>We need to use fastballs here and get some strikes.</i>

00:11:58.150 --> 00:11:59.230
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:08.450
Ball... four!

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.150
<i>No out and the bases are loaded.</i>

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:13.960
Time, please.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:17.090
Um, are you okay?

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:18.280
No problems.

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:19.830
It's as it always is.

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:21.670
The beginning of games are like this.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:22.770
But...

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:25.640
Well, I'm telling you not to worry.

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:32.490
Play!

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:54.550
This is a free fansub.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:54.550
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:12:59.500
Out!

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.750
Go!

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:04.300
Safe!

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:16.770
Out!

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:18.310
Out!

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:27.610
Hey, hey! Why do you look so worried?{are you making such a troubled face?}

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:29.820
We've only given up one run so far.

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:33.020
We'll get it back in no time.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:35.330
Yes!

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:36.610
<i>That's right.</i>

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:38.210
<i>I don't have time to be depressed.</i>

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:41.910
<i>I need to think about how I can hold them back in the next inning.</i>

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:45.060
<i>I won't be excused if I screw up more.</i>

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:09.780
Safe!

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:16.130
All right!

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:23.050
Out!

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:28.720
We're tied now!

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.390
Okay, it begins for real now!

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.900
Let's do our best!

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:33.850
Yes!

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:48.910
Out!

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:54.600
<i>It's important to get outs one by one for now.</i>

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:58.160
Batting eighth: third baseman, Yakushiji.

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:05.340
<i>He seemed to be in good form during batting practice, but...</i>

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:08.210
<i>I know exactly what location he's bad with.</i>

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:14.670
<i>What?</i>

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:21.480
<i>W-We'll study the situation with a curve first.</i>

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:23.980
<i>W-We'll study the situation with a curve first.</i>

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:34.740
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:40.910
Safe!

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:43.880
<i>Okay!</i>

00:15:57.820 --> 00:15:58.510
Safe!

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:03.700
Batting eighth: catcher, Sato.

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:06.150
Toshi-kun!

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.360
Do your best!

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:12.140
It's Toshiya's turn!

00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:13.030
Yeah.

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:15.870
This is an important chance for him.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:21.040
<i>No matter what, I have to get the runner home!</i>

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:25.250
<i>This battery closes in on hitters with fastballs most of the time.</i>

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:27.680
<i>I'll challenge them with all my strength on the first pitch!</i>

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:40.720
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.210
All right! All right!

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:45.020
Out!

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:57.090
Well, if you enter the batter's box with such a strong intent to hit it...

00:16:57.090 --> 00:16:59.240
of course you'll get out.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.880
Don't mind, don't mind!

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:01.660
We'll get it back! {sangofe guess on whta kohn didnt hear}

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:03.710
Toshiya!

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:15.600
<i>Runners on second and third and now Brightman!</i>

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:17.310
<i>And he's already gotten a hit!</i>

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:21.760
<i>The next batter hit into a lot of double plays last season.</i>

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.110
<i>Here we'll...</i>

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:26.710
Time, please.

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:28.350
Time!

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:31.110
He's going to confirm loading the bases?

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:36.290
This won't work. That catcher is completely ready to flee.

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:41.780
The genius rookie that I expected so much from is only this good?

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:43.790
This is kind of a let-down.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:46.500
<i>Sato...</i>

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:52.300
Brightman can hit your curveballs that go off course where he wants them.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:55.480
We should load the bases and challenge the next batter.

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:58.680
No, let me challenge him.

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:02.100
It's because he hit my ball that I want to challenge him again.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.220
This time I'll definitely hold him back!

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.850
But... if you fail...

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:10.340
It's better to regret after trying than regret not having tried.

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:13.860
If I fail, then I fail. That'll be a good experience too.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.670
It'll help me the next time.

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:18.650
Well, just trust me.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:22.350
You have to go through these kinds of situations many, many times, after all.

00:18:24.690 --> 00:18:26.040
I understand.

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:41.180
Strike!

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:43.390
His slider hit perfectly!

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:50.100
Strike!

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:57.820
Strike! Batter out!

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:08.450
Strike! Batter out!

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:14.100
All right!

00:19:15.530 --> 00:19:16.630
All right!

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:18.820
Out!

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:31.770
That's how someone baptized as a pro does things, rookie.

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.260
Hey, hey, what are you saying?

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:35.440
Yatabe-chan.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.570
He's holding them back nicely, isn't he?

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:39.990
With Iwai's lead.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:43.240
W-Well, that may be true, but...

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.320
It's as Yatabe-san says.

00:19:45.320 --> 00:19:46.270
Sato.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:50.830
Neither my lead nor my swing are at the pro level yet.

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:54.250
Coming here was still too early.

00:19:54.930 --> 00:19:56.710
Before piling up all these mistakes,

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:58.930
I should have known that.

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:04.090
It seems like you don't get the meaning of what I said at all!

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:09.130
Didn't you realize something while watching Iwai?

00:20:09.130 --> 00:20:14.790
He's supposed to have taught you an important thing that you had forgotten.

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:16.020
An important thing?

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:20.560
<i>It's because he hit my ball that I want to challenge him again.</i>

00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:22.570
<i>This time I'll definitely hold him back!</i>

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:26.280
<i>It's better to regret after trying than regret not having tried.</i>

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:31.050
<i>If I fail, then I fail. That'll be a good experience too.</i>

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:33.380
<i>It'll help me the next time.</i>

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:37.810
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:40.430
<i>A pro who plays many games over a long season...</i>

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:44.090
<i>can't continue piling up mistakes forever!</i>

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.760
Batting eighth: third baseman, Yakushiji.

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:55.130
<i>If I make a mistake, I just need to make sure it prepares me for the next time!</i>

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:57.400
<i>I have to press forward with my eyes straight ahead!</i>

00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:03.320
<i>Yes, since right now I'm a challenger!</i>

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:08.950
Strike!

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:12.930
<i>A fastball on the corner.</i>

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:16.370
<i>At last he's returned to his usual self, making a strong lead.</i>

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:21.500
It seems that you finally understand.

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:32.190
Foul!

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:34.640
<i>Next time we'll use a sneaky location.</i>

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:39.110
Foul!

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:41.110
<i>As I expected.</i>

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:43.200
<i>He reacted in an instant and managed to hit it.</i>

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:49.450
<i>They attacked with fastballs inside twice in a row...</i>

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:51.590
<i>and retreated with a curveball outside on the following pitch.</i>

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:52.910
<i>Next is...</i>

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:54.750
<i>undoubtedly a fastball!</i>

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:01.640
<i>Wha-</i>

00:22:04.220 --> 00:22:05.420
Damn it!

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:13.890
Toshiya!

00:22:16.540 --> 00:22:17.600
Out!

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:19.650
Nice going, Toshiya!

00:22:24.880 --> 00:22:26.860
One out! One out!

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:30.740
I can't be off-guard now either.

00:22:34.590 --> 00:22:37.700
<i>Well then, this is the real start of the game!</i>

00:24:10.770 --> 00:24:14.510
In Japan, the time for graduation ceremonies was getting closer.

00:24:14.510 --> 00:24:18.970
Everyone is following their respective roads and doing their best, right?

00:24:18.970 --> 00:24:22.530
All right, I'll put everything into it and do my best too!

00:24:22.530 --> 00:24:23.780
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.780 --> 00:24:25.190
It's Not Impossible.

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:27.990
Run to the stage of your dreams!
